  'pub.fact.instagram.1': 'There is an official publishing API for Instagram professional accounts (Business and Creator): images, videos/Reels and carousels.',
  'pub.fact.instagram.2': 'The flow has two steps: create a media container and publish it. Reels use the REELS type.',
  'pub.fact.instagram.3': 'The media must be at a public address at the time of the attempt, or be sent by resumable upload (only for apps with Facebook Login for Business).',
  'pub.fact.instagram.4': 'Reported limit: 100 API-published posts per 24 hours per account.',
  'pub.fact.instagram.5': 'Requires a Meta app with publishing permissions (for example instagram_business_content_publish or instagram_content_publish), Standard and Advanced access levels and, when the Page requires it, Page Publishing Authorization (PPA).',
  'pub.fact.instagram.6': 'Scheduling through the API: not found in the documentation consulted. Meta recommends the app itself enforce the limit when scheduling future posts.',
  'pub.fact.facebook.1': 'The official Reels API publishes only to Facebook Pages (not to personal profiles).',
  'pub.fact.facebook.2': 'Three-step flow: start the upload session, upload the video and publish.',
  'pub.fact.facebook.3': 'Video: .mp4 recommended, 9:16 aspect ratio, 1080×1920 recommended (minimum 540×960), 24 to 60 frames per second and 3 to 90 seconds long.',
  'pub.fact.facebook.4': 'Reported limit: 30 API-published Reels per 24 hours.',
  'pub.fact.facebook.5': 'Permissions: pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement and pages_manage_posts, with a Page token from someone who can create content on it.',
  'pub.fact.facebook.6': 'The user must be shown how their Reels will be used and the chosen audience (for Pages, Public only).',
  'pub.fact.facebook.7': 'Reels scheduling: the official page consulted does not describe it; third-party sources disagree. XFLUX should do its own scheduling.',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.1': 'The official Content Posting API has "Direct Post" (posts to the profile, scope video.publish) and "Upload" (sends to the app inbox, where the creator finishes; scope video.upload).',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.2': 'Unaudited apps can only post privately. The audit is what unlocks public visibility.',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.3': 'The guidelines require, for every post: fetching the creator’s options, showing the account name, the user choosing privacy manually (no default) and consenting before upload.',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.4': 'The usage guidelines list as not acceptable a tool that only helps upload content to accounts you or your team manage. This must be assessed in the audit.',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.5': 'Reported limits: 6 requests per minute per token and a daily post cap per creator (around 15, shared across apps).',
  'pub.fact.tiktok.6': 'Scheduling through the API: not found in the documentation consulted.',
  'pub.fact.shopee.1': 'Shopee Open Platform has official APIs to upload videos to a shop’s media space (used in product listings), 10 to 60 seconds long.',
  'pub.fact.shopee.2': 'There is a "Video" module (v2.video) with user-level authorization and the app type "Shopee Video Management". The sources consulted showed operations to list, get details and edit information.',
  'pub.fact.shopee.3': 'We could not confirm a public official API to PUBLISH on Shopee Video. Partner ERPs advertise publishing and scheduling, but this was not confirmed in the documentation.',
  'pub.fact.shopee.4': 'That is why XFLUX keeps Shopee Video as assisted posting until the official documentation and a partner account confirm this possibility.',
  'pub.fact.pinterest.1': 'API v5 creates video Pins: register the video, upload it and create the Pin with it. Every Pin lives on a board.',
  'pub.fact.pinterest.2': 'Developer guides cite the scopes boards:read, boards:write, pins:read and pins:write. Confirm in the official reference when implementing.',
  'pub.fact.pinterest.3': 'Trial access: created Pins are visible only to the creator and only the app owner’s account can authorize. Standard access requires app review.',
  'pub.fact.pinterest.4': 'Scheduling through the API: not found in the sources consulted.',
  'pub.fact.youtube.1': 'The official API uses the videos.insert method (scope youtube.upload). The reference lists no Shorts field: YouTube itself classifies the video as a Short.',
  'pub.fact.youtube.2': 'Reported quota: 100 uploads per day per project, each costing 1 unit in the "Video Uploads" bucket.',
  'pub.fact.youtube.3': 'Scheduling: the upload accepts the status.publishAt field.',
  'pub.fact.youtube.4': 'If privacy is not set, the default is public. The current official page says videos from unverified projects are not restricted to private mode; old versions and third-party guides say otherwise. Confirm before launch.',
  'pub.fact.youtube.5': 'The YouTube API Terms of Service and Developer Policies apply; a compliance audit may be needed to raise quota.',
